1
00:00:51,670 --> 00:00:52,670
Unload the cargo.

2
00:01:14,750 --> 00:01:16,230
Heard the goods are pretty good today.

3
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,000
The goods are here.

4
00:03:10,330 --> 00:03:12,250
What beautiful eyes.

5
00:03:13,380 --> 00:03:14,380
What are you waiting for.

6
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:15,920
Don't waste her.

7
00:03:39,420 --> 00:03:40,829
This chick's kind of interesting.

8
00:03:47,170 --> 00:03:49,040
Rest assured I'll sell you a good price.

9
00:04:07,250 --> 00:04:08,250
Fuck.

10
00:04:40,580 --> 00:04:41,880
True top.

11
00:06:32,290 --> 00:06:33,290
You.

12
00:06:34,290 --> 00:06:35,420
Who are you guys.

13
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:43,880
Old Man's men.

14
00:06:52,500 --> 00:06:53,960
Thank you for saving us.

15
00:06:54,750 --> 00:06:55,250
You're welcome.

16
00:06:55,420 --> 00:06:56,420
Thanks.

17
00:07:07,540 --> 00:07:08,580
Time to clean up the trash.

18
00:08:15,580 --> 00:08:16,580
What are you doing.

19
00:08:16,710 --> 00:08:17,710
Cleaning up the trash.

20
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:22,500
Bodies.

21
00:08:22,880 --> 00:08:23,880
Weapons.

22
00:08:24,920 --> 00:08:26,170
And these little scraps.

23
00:08:27,290 --> 00:08:28,290
Blow 'em all up.

24
00:08:36,289 --> 00:08:38,750
Old Man's rule: Leave no loose ends.

25
00:08:39,250 --> 00:08:41,620
A bunch of kids—what threat are they.

26
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:45,420
Being alive is a threat.

27
00:08:47,170 --> 00:08:48,710
If other traffickers catch 'em.

28
00:08:49,830 --> 00:08:51,000
Their fate'll be even worse.

29
00:08:54,460 --> 00:08:58,000
Better to die quick. Than live in pain.

30
00:09:00,620 --> 00:09:02,040
Touch bomb—one touch and it blows.

31
00:09:11,120 --> 00:09:13,290
Break Old Man's rules, and we all die.

32
00:09:13,540 --> 00:09:14,580
Cut the crap.

33
00:09:20,210 --> 00:09:21,210
We're running out of time.

34
00:09:21,830 --> 00:09:22,516
Have fun by yourself.

35
00:09:22,540 --> 00:09:23,540
Get back.

36
00:10:52,880 --> 00:10:53,880
This shop.

37
00:10:54,380 --> 00:10:56,460
Only the blind girl and her sister run it.

38
00:12:19,880 --> 00:12:20,880
What are you doing.

39
00:12:22,620 --> 00:12:24,460
What's going on sister.

40
00:12:24,620 --> 00:12:26,120
Easy, easy, don't panic.

41
00:12:26,380 --> 00:12:27,420
We brothers.

42
00:12:27,790 --> 00:12:29,250
Starting on the first of this month.

43
00:12:29,750 --> 00:12:31,056
We're here to collect protection money.

44
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:32,080
Not much.

45
00:12:32,210 --> 00:12:33,210
Fifty grand.

46
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:39,080
Okay I'll pay you.

47
00:12:39,120 --> 00:12:40,120
Let's talk outside.

48
00:12:41,420 --> 00:12:42,420
That easy.

49
00:12:43,750 --> 00:12:45,710
Should I ask for interest, then.

50
00:12:49,540 --> 00:12:50,000
Let go of me.

51
00:12:50,080 --> 00:12:51,420
Never tried a blind girl before.

52
00:12:53,670 --> 00:12:54,880
Hi, Sister.

53
00:13:02,210 --> 00:13:03,210
Come here.

54
00:13:23,210 --> 00:13:23,880
Hello.

55
00:13:23,920 --> 00:13:24,920
This is 911.

56
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:26,210
How may I help you.

57
00:13:29,540 --> 00:13:30,830
We've located your phone.

58
00:13:31,040 --> 00:13:32,160
Please keep the line open.

59
00:13:43,830 --> 00:13:44,830
I'll fucking kill you.

60
00:14:37,330 --> 00:14:38,330
Badge number 9501.

61
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:39,356
A murder case occurred on Nanyang Street.

62
00:14:39,380 --> 00:14:40,380
Request support.

63
00:14:40,830 --> 00:14:41,330
Sister.

64
00:14:41,670 --> 00:14:42,080
Sister.

65
00:14:42,170 --> 00:14:43,170
Are you okay.

66
00:14:43,420 --> 00:14:44,000
It's okay.

67
00:14:44,420 --> 00:14:45,420
Don't be afraid.

68
00:14:57,250 --> 00:14:58,670
Those were just standard procedures.

69
00:14:58,750 --> 00:14:59,880
That's why it was formal.

70
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:01,000
No need to be nervous.

71
00:15:08,210 --> 00:15:13,290
The major Nancheng train accident three years ago you two were on that train.

72
00:15:14,620 --> 00:15:15,000
Yes.

73
00:15:15,420 --> 00:15:17,540
My sister saved thirteen people in the carriage.

74
00:15:17,750 --> 00:15:19,500
Many reporters wanted to interview her.

75
00:15:19,880 --> 00:15:21,000
But she refused all of them.

76
00:15:22,750 --> 00:15:24,830
Fame is a good thing. Why refuse.

77
00:15:27,330 --> 00:15:28,460
It was just a disaster.

78
00:15:28,750 --> 00:15:29,830
Nothing to brag about.

79
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:39,080
Help.

80
00:15:39,500 --> 00:15:40,500
Mingzhu, don't be afraid.

81
00:15:40,620 --> 00:15:41,330
Sister.

82
00:15:41,580 --> 00:15:42,580
Is it you.

83
00:15:44,620 --> 00:15:45,620
A blessing in disguise.

84
00:15:45,880 --> 00:15:48,750
Heaven let me meet my sister in that accident.

85
00:15:50,210 --> 00:15:52,840
If not for my sister I can't go to a school for the blind either.

86
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:56,920
Did you open the coffee shop together.

87
00:15:57,170 --> 00:15:58,170
Yeah.

88
00:15:59,540 --> 00:16:00,540
You can too.

89
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:03,380
My sister puts things in fixed places

90
00:16:03,540 --> 00:16:04,740
I know where they are by touch.

91
00:16:10,620 --> 00:16:11,000
Sir.

92
00:16:11,120 --> 00:16:11,670
Confirmed.

93
00:16:11,750 --> 00:16:12,896
The one who escaped is Poison Rat

94
00:16:12,920 --> 00:16:14,600
I think we can issue a warrant immediately.

95
00:16:16,880 --> 00:16:20,120
Without solid evidence don't alert the enemy.

96
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:27,000
Sir...

97
00:16:27,040 --> 00:16:28,040
Can we leave now.

98
00:16:29,960 --> 00:16:30,460
Yes.

99
00:16:30,670 --> 00:16:31,670
Keep your phone on.

100
00:16:33,330 --> 00:16:34,920
Sister, are you hurt.

101
00:16:35,460 --> 00:16:36,460
I'm fine.

102
00:16:37,290 --> 00:16:38,290
But.

103
00:16:38,620 --> 00:16:40,290
Why are you home so early today.

104
00:16:41,790 --> 00:16:43,750
I wanted to surprise you

105
00:16:43,880 --> 00:16:45,540
I didn't expect this to happen.

106
00:16:46,210 --> 00:16:47,750
Luckily the police came in time.

107
00:16:49,080 --> 00:16:49,960
But.

108
00:16:50,080 --> 00:16:51,620
Next time you come home.

109
00:16:52,040 --> 00:16:53,420
Tell me in advance.

110
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:55,880
Got it.

111
00:16:58,330 --> 00:16:59,000
Mingzhu.

112
00:16:59,250 --> 00:17:00,356
There's a little beggar behind us.

113
00:17:00,380 --> 00:17:02,540
Wait here for a moment I'll go give him some change.

114
00:17:03,290 --> 00:17:04,290
Wait here for me.

115
00:17:09,290 --> 00:17:10,290
Bold move.

116
00:17:10,540 --> 00:17:11,920
Let's talk over there.

117
00:17:21,079 --> 00:17:22,500
Nice spot you picked.

118
00:17:24,210 --> 00:17:25,710
I picked it just for you.

119
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:32,880
Tell my brothers what you have to say.

120
00:17:44,670 --> 00:17:45,670
Sister.

121
00:17:47,290 --> 00:17:48,290
I'm here.

122
00:17:53,750 --> 00:17:55,120
I have change too.

123
00:17:56,670 --> 00:17:57,710
He's already gone.

124
00:18:00,460 --> 00:18:01,790
Let's go home.

125
00:18:03,670 --> 00:18:04,670
Mingzhu.

126
00:18:05,080 --> 00:18:07,290
Go to Aunt Chen's and buy me some guangbing

127
00:18:07,420 --> 00:18:08,960
I have to clean the equipment tonight.

128
00:18:09,420 --> 00:18:11,460
You finally let me go out alone

129
00:18:11,580 --> 00:18:12,580
I'm leaving then.

130
00:18:12,790 --> 00:18:13,790
Be careful.

131
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:14,880
Okay.

132
00:18:27,250 --> 00:18:28,970
I suspect this isn't a simple disappearance.

133
00:18:29,040 --> 00:18:31,250
Poison Rat knows too much.

134
00:18:31,620 --> 00:18:34,790
This case could be a breakthrough.

135
00:18:34,830 --> 00:18:36,470
To crack the cross-border crime syndicate.

136
00:18:40,670 --> 00:18:42,230
We're not the only ones looking for him.

137
00:18:42,330 --> 00:18:44,080
Several other forces have their eyes on him.

138
00:18:44,460 --> 00:18:45,460
Insufficient evidence.

139
00:18:45,540 --> 00:18:46,540
Clues are lost.

140
00:18:46,670 --> 00:18:48,470
Further investigation is a waste of resources.

141
00:18:49,080 --> 00:18:50,080
Close the case.

142
00:18:50,620 --> 00:18:51,620
Close it.

143
00:18:52,040 --> 00:18:54,670
If we let this clue go we'll never get close again.

144
00:18:54,920 --> 00:18:56,000
You're a cop.

145
00:18:56,500 --> 00:18:57,580
You must follow orders.

146
00:18:57,620 --> 00:18:59,120
If we don't investigate, who will.

147
00:19:03,790 --> 00:19:06,320
I don't want you to end up like your father.

148
00:19:06,420 --> 00:19:08,920
He threw himself into cases and lost his life.

149
00:19:10,420 --> 00:19:11,500
You're still young.

150
00:19:18,120 --> 00:19:19,360
I won't sign the closure report.

151
00:19:22,710 --> 00:19:26,170
By ten tomorrow morning I want the case files on my desk.

152
00:19:36,580 --> 00:19:39,830
There have been multiple homicides in the city recently.

153
00:19:40,830 --> 00:19:45,620
Police suspect a professional assassin organization is behind these murders.

154
00:19:46,790 --> 00:19:49,290
The organization uses cruel methods.

155
00:19:49,670 --> 00:19:51,210
Leaving no survivors.

156
00:19:51,460 --> 00:19:57,250
They're also suspected of. Colluding with local criminal gangs to carry out targeted assassinations.

157
00:20:07,040 --> 00:20:08,040
Hello.

158
00:20:08,380 --> 00:20:10,186
Check the surveillance near the coffee shop again for me.

159
00:20:10,210 --> 00:20:11,380
Any leads on Poison Rat.

160
00:20:56,790 --> 00:21:00,250
Beautiful, kind lovely and excellent Ms. Minghui.

161
00:21:00,620 --> 00:21:03,330
Your delivery has arrived safely.

162
00:21:04,170 --> 00:21:05,170
You're back.

163
00:21:07,540 --> 00:21:08,710
Let's have dinner first.

164
00:21:13,710 --> 00:21:15,040
It smells good.

165
00:21:16,080 --> 00:21:20,210
If you don't come eat your guangbing will be in Mingzhu's belly.

166
00:21:22,710 --> 00:21:24,350
I'm still cleaning the equipment, Mingzhu

167
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:25,920
I'll bring it down to you.

168
00:21:26,330 --> 00:21:27,040
Don't come down.

169
00:21:27,120 --> 00:21:28,120
The floor is slippery.

170
00:21:31,790 --> 00:21:32,380
It's okay

171
00:21:32,660 --> 00:21:33,710
I'll wait here for you.

172
00:21:37,460 --> 00:21:38,460
Sister.

173
00:21:38,830 --> 00:21:42,250
Do you remember. When we were at the orphanage

174
00:21:42,580 --> 00:21:43,830
I was always hungry.

175
00:21:44,500 --> 00:21:48,790
Every time my stomach growled you'd always magically get me guangbing.

176
00:21:50,670 --> 00:21:56,170
Back then, I really thought guangbing was the most delicious thing in the world.

177
00:21:59,120 --> 00:22:00,540
Mingzhu, here's your guangbing.

178
00:22:05,620 --> 00:22:07,670
Eat slowly, don't choke.

179
00:22:07,880 --> 00:22:08,580
Sister.

180
00:22:08,710 --> 00:22:09,710
You eat too.

181
00:22:10,380 --> 00:22:11,670
I'm full.

182
00:22:15,040 --> 00:22:16,040
You eat.

183
00:22:16,710 --> 00:22:18,250
Later I found out.

184
00:22:18,750 --> 00:22:22,330
Those flatbreads who got these back every time you got beaten.

185
00:22:23,790 --> 00:22:24,250
Sister.

186
00:22:24,580 --> 00:22:25,580
Are you listening.

187
00:22:26,330 --> 00:22:27,330
I'm listening.

188
00:22:30,210 --> 00:22:35,040
After you left my birthday wish every year was for you to come back.

189
00:22:36,080 --> 00:22:39,120
Today is the third anniversary of our reunion.

190
00:22:40,790 --> 00:22:41,380
Sister.

191
00:22:41,750 --> 00:22:43,080
We'll never be apart again.

192
00:22:43,540 --> 00:22:44,540
Right.

193
00:22:47,920 --> 00:22:48,920
Yes.

194
00:22:49,380 --> 00:22:50,380
Never again.

195
00:22:54,170 --> 00:22:54,830
Sister.

196
00:22:55,120 --> 00:22:57,500
All these years were you alone too.

197
00:22:58,710 --> 00:23:01,580
Someone adopted me and some other kids.

198
00:23:02,420 --> 00:23:03,580
We called him Old Man.

199
00:23:09,040 --> 00:23:10,120
Stay in formation.

200
00:23:11,750 --> 00:23:13,250
Hang onto the rope.

201
00:23:19,080 --> 00:23:20,250
Check your weapons.

202
00:23:20,460 --> 00:23:21,580
Then push forward with force.

203
00:23:25,670 --> 00:23:26,670
Ladies.

204
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:29,120
Stay low in the water, goddammit.

205
00:23:29,620 --> 00:23:30,790
Keep your heads down.

206
00:23:33,170 --> 00:23:33,880
Good, good.

207
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:35,000
Pull harder.

208
00:23:35,210 --> 00:23:38,250
Close combat, yes, good.

209
00:23:38,380 --> 00:23:39,670
Excellent.

210
00:23:56,290 --> 00:23:58,396
Our goal is to become.

211
00:23:58,420 --> 00:24:00,040
The deadliest weapons in the world.

212
00:24:00,790 --> 00:24:02,670
The most elite and capable.

213
00:24:03,210 --> 00:24:06,790
This is the only way we survive in this damn world.

214
00:24:06,960 --> 00:24:07,960
Understand.

215
00:24:08,040 --> 00:24:09,290
Yes, Old Man.

216
00:24:09,460 --> 00:24:10,460
What are we.

217
00:24:11,040 --> 00:24:11,920
Family.

218
00:24:12,040 --> 00:24:13,880
What must you always remember.

219
00:24:14,460 --> 00:24:15,670
Never part.

220
00:24:25,670 --> 00:24:27,670
Don't go soft just because she's your sister.

221
00:24:42,040 --> 00:24:43,580
This is your killer instinct

222
00:25:20,580 --> 00:25:21,580
children.

223
00:25:22,330 --> 00:25:22,920
Today.

224
00:25:23,080 --> 00:25:25,330
It is to help you learn.

225
00:25:25,540 --> 00:25:28,330
In no circumstances can we relax our vigilance.

226
00:25:29,620 --> 00:25:33,790
I want to see you all. How to Turn the Tables in Adversity.

227
00:25:33,920 --> 00:25:34,920
Go back.

228
00:25:35,710 --> 00:25:36,710
Hold her down.

229
00:25:50,420 --> 00:25:51,420
Tide.

230
00:25:52,080 --> 00:25:53,080
You are excellent.

231
00:25:53,540 --> 00:25:55,790
But you need to learn to solve problems on your own.

232
00:25:55,960 --> 00:25:57,080
You are now protecting her.

233
00:25:58,750 --> 00:26:00,500
It's also destroying oneself.

234
00:26:01,460 --> 00:26:02,460
Lock her up.

235
00:26:41,250 --> 00:26:42,250
Eat quickly.

236
00:26:52,000 --> 00:26:53,000
Slow down.

237
00:26:59,290 --> 00:27:00,290
Thank you.

238
00:27:06,040 --> 00:27:07,640
Have you ever thought about leaving here.

239
00:27:11,620 --> 00:27:12,620
Yes.

240
00:27:16,120 --> 00:27:17,290
But I have to survive first.

241
00:27:19,540 --> 00:27:21,250
Where will you go when you leave.

242
00:27:24,620 --> 00:27:25,620
Find my sister.

243
00:27:26,380 --> 00:27:27,420
She's blind.

244
00:27:28,210 --> 00:27:29,250
I'm very worried about her.

245
00:27:31,420 --> 00:27:32,420
What about you.

246
00:27:37,120 --> 00:27:39,170
Me I don't know.

247
00:27:41,330 --> 00:27:42,330
Where's your family.

248
00:27:51,750 --> 00:27:52,750
Then from now on

249
00:27:54,330 --> 00:27:55,500
I'll be your sister.

250
00:29:45,620 --> 00:29:46,710
We grew up together.

251
00:29:47,040 --> 00:29:48,330
No one was ever left behind.

252
00:29:49,170 --> 00:29:51,980
After you came back do you still keep in touch with them.

253
00:29:53,920 --> 00:29:54,920
No.

254
00:29:55,330 --> 00:29:57,420
We went our separate ways after we grew up.

255
00:29:59,120 --> 00:30:02,670
If he saw how happy I am he'd be happy for me.

256
00:30:05,420 --> 00:30:06,000
Sister.

257
00:30:06,420 --> 00:30:08,900
All these years have you been through a lot alone.

258
00:30:11,540 --> 00:30:14,710
As long as you're by my side everything is worth it.

259
00:30:38,080 --> 00:30:39,080
Class dismissed.

260
00:30:40,830 --> 00:30:41,830
Slow down.

261
00:30:48,040 --> 00:30:49,800
The legislators are very satisfied with you.

262
00:30:50,120 --> 00:30:52,540
These campaign obstacles were all handled very smoothly.

263
00:30:53,380 --> 00:30:55,960
But there's one loose end.

264
00:30:56,880 --> 00:30:57,976
There was a person named Tooru-ji.

265
00:30:58,000 --> 00:30:59,290
Know a lot of things about us.

266
00:30:59,620 --> 00:31:01,420
He caused trouble and disappeared.

267
00:31:01,670 --> 00:31:05,710
If Someone else finds him it'll be bad for us.

268
00:31:09,960 --> 00:31:11,120
Dig him out for me.

269
00:31:17,750 --> 00:31:19,210
Where was he last seen.

270
00:31:20,290 --> 00:31:21,460
Your coffee is ready.

271
00:31:21,670 --> 00:31:22,186
Thank you.

272
00:31:22,210 --> 00:31:22,976
You waited for me so late

273
00:31:23,000 --> 00:31:23,596
I'm leaving now.

274
00:31:23,620 --> 00:31:24,080
Bye.

275
00:31:24,120 --> 00:31:25,250
Bye, take care.

276
00:31:34,290 --> 00:31:36,000
Sorry, we're closed.

277
00:31:46,790 --> 00:31:47,790
Hello.

278
00:31:48,210 --> 00:31:49,380
Are you alone here.

279
00:31:50,120 --> 00:31:51,000
My sister is here too.

280
00:31:51,080 --> 00:31:52,080
She'll be back soon.

281
00:31:58,330 --> 00:32:00,330
Can I help you with something.

282
00:32:02,040 --> 00:32:03,040
Looking for someone.

283
00:32:05,330 --> 00:32:06,330
Who.

284
00:32:14,420 --> 00:32:15,420
The person in this photo.

285
00:32:16,880 --> 00:32:18,170
Is this your sister.

286
00:32:19,750 --> 00:32:20,750
Yes.

287
00:32:24,580 --> 00:32:25,580
What's her name.

288
00:32:26,290 --> 00:32:27,290
Minghui.

289
00:32:27,580 --> 00:32:28,580
Do you know her.

290
00:32:31,210 --> 00:32:32,210
